  "name": "Cham music of Ninh Thuận (Katê festival and ritual music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the Cham of Ninh Thuận and Bình Thuận on Vietnam's south-central coast, heard at the Katê festival at the Po Klong Garai and Po Rome towers and at life-cycle rites. Its core ensemble pairs the saranai shawm with the double-headed ginăng drum and the single-headed baranưng frame drum, accompanying ritual dance. The serunai card stands in for the saranai, and generic membrane-drum and frame-drum cards for the ginăng and baranưng.",
  "recipe": "classic modern cham music of ninh thuận, ritual Devotional, indigenous branch. serunai shawm, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, credited frame drums. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
